Z||000010||TOM||04-22-2000||10:44 AM||||This is what the seller sent me.<P>However, it's widely known that GM took controlling stock in Group Lotus in <BR>Jan. 1986, and the new suspension cost GM/Pontiac Division an estimated $30 <BR>million to redesign.<P>Though it doesn't actually say "lotus" in the '88 presskit or 4 published <BR>'88 dealer brochures, It is menioned in the Aug. 1995 High Performance <BR>Pontiac on pg. 21, and in an 88 Motor Trend.<P>Here is a link to the Aug. HPP:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.org/text/hpp1.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.org/text/hpp1.html</A> <P>I (and the 500+ Fiero sites and the Fiero Stores' ads) may all be victims of <BR>a long standing rumor.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||WKDFIRO||04-24-2000||05:45 AM||||The suspension in the 88 Fieros was actually on the drawing boards at the beginning. The bean counters wanted off the shelf suspension for a cheaper price to bump up the bottom line. And actually a lot of the things found in a Fiero were found when engineers went and looked at the Fiat X-19. For instance, the roof of the Fiat also happen to fit perfectly under the front hood.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Haze_Performance||04-25-2000||01:44 AM||||I had a 1979 Fiat Bertone X/19 with a targa top.Ugly lime green with brown/tan int. I just thought I would share that info..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||Standard||04-25-2000||02:25 AM||||Hulki Aldicati himself said that the "lotus-designed suspension" was just a rumour.||||reg||1
Z||000014||terryk||04-25-2000||06:52 PM||||Lotus "inspired" maybe, but not Lotus designed. The 88 design was the "original" design. <P>Old rumors die hard.<P>The 88 suspension was removed to get the base price of the car back down to the $6k range.<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 04-25-2000).]||||reg||1
